    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# What Is Static Analysis? — AI Security Demonstration\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook shows **why static analysis matters for AI/ML code**.\n",
        "\n",
        "We walk through three examples of code that:\n",
        "- ✅ Pass unit tests\n",
        "- ✅ Work correctly with “happy path” inputs\n",
        "- ❌ Still contain serious security vulnerabilities\n",
        "\n",
        "Static analysis is about finding **security issues in code structure and patterns**, not just bugs that appear at runtime.\n"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Imports\n",
        "\n",
        "We’ll use a few standard ML and data libraries to simulate realistic AI code.\n"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import os\n",
        "import pickle\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\"*70)\n",
        "print(\"STATIC ANALYSIS DEMONSTRATION\")\n",
        "print(\"Running code examples that pass tests but have security issues\")\n",
        "print(\"=\"*70)"
      ]
    },

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */
    /* EXAMPLE 1: DATA LOADING WITHOUT VALIDATION                    */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Example 1 — Data Loading Without Validation\n",
        "\n",
        "### What this is meant to teach\n",
        "- Unit tests often use **small, trusted test files**.\n",
        "- In production, the same function may load **untrusted, large, or malicious data**.\n",
        "- Static analysis can flag **missing validation and checks** that tests never exercise.\n",
        "\n",
        "We’ll define a `load_training_data` function that passes tests but is insecure.\n"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def load_training_data(file_path):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Loads training data from CSV file.\n",
        "    \n",
        "    ✅ PASSES TESTS: Works correctly with valid inputs.\n",
        "    ❌ SECURITY ISSUES: No validation, size limits, or integrity checks.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    df = pd.read_csv(file_path)\n",
        "    return df\n",
        "\n",
        "def test_load_training_data():\n",
        "    \"\"\"Unit test that passes because it uses a small, trusted test file.\"\"\"\n",
        "    test_data = pd.DataFrame({\"feature1\": [1, 2, 3], \"label\": [0, 1, 0]})\n",
        "    test_data.to_csv(\"test_data.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "    \n",        
        "    result = load_training_data(\"test_data.csv\")\n",
        "    assert len(result) == 3\n",
        "    assert \"feature1\" in result.columns\n",
        "    print(\"✓ Unit test PASSED for load_training_data\")\n",
        "    \n",
        "    os.remove(\"test_data.csv\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*70)\n",
        "print(\"EXAMPLE 1: DATA LOADING FUNCTION\")\n",
        "print(\"=\"*70)\n",
        "print(\"\\n[Running unit test...]\")\n",
        "test_load_training_data()"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### What static analysis would flag here\n",
        "\n",
        "Static analysis tools don’t just ask “does it work?” — they ask:\n",
        "- Is there **input validation**?\n",
        "- Are there **size limits**?\n",
        "- Is there **integrity checking**?\n",
        "- Could this function be abused in production?\n"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"\\n[What Static Analysis Would Flag:]\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  WARNING: No validation on file_path parameter\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  WARNING: No file size limit checking\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  WARNING: No data integrity verification (checksums/signatures)\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  WARNING: No anomaly detection in loaded data\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  WARNING: Could load malicious/poisoned data in production\")\n",
        "print(\"\\n🔍 Static analysis finds structural security issues that tests never touch.\")"
      ]
    },

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */
    /* EXAMPLE 2: MODEL LOADING WITH PATH TRAVERSAL + PICKLE         */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Example 2 — Model Loading with Path Traversal & Unsafe Deserialization\n",
        "\n",
        "### What this is meant to teach\n",
        "- User-controlled input used in file paths can lead to **path traversal**.\n",
        "- Using `pickle.load()` on files derived from user input is **extremely dangerous**.\n",
        "- Unit tests that use only safe model names will **never see the vulnerability**.\n",
        "\n",
        "We’ll define a `load_and_predict` function that passes tests but is critically insecure.\n"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def load_and_predict(model_name, input_data):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Loads model and returns prediction.\n",
        "    \n",
        "    ✅ PASSES TESTS: Works with valid model names.\n",
        "    ❌ SECURITY ISSUE: Path traversal + unsafe pickle deserialization.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    # User-controlled input directly used in file path\n",
        "    model_path = f\"models/{model_name}.pkl\"\n",
        "    \n",
        "    with open(model_path, \"rb\") as f:\n",
        "        model = pickle.load(f)  # unsafe deserialization\n",
        "    \n",
        "    prediction = model.predict(input_data)\n",
        "    return prediction\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*70)\n",
        "print(\"EXAMPLE 2: MODEL SERVING API\")\n",
        "print(\"=\"*70)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[Setting up test environment...]\")\n",
        "os.makedirs(\"models\", exist_ok=True)\n",
        "dummy_model = LogisticRegression()\n",
        "dummy_model.fit(np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4]]), np.array([0, 1]))\n",
        "with open(\"models/test_model.pkl\", \"wb\") as f:\n",
        "    pickle.dump(dummy_model, f)\n",
        "\n",
        "def test_load_and_predict():\n",
        "    \"\"\"Unit test passes with legitimate model name.\"\"\"\n",
        "    input_data = np.array([[2, 3]])\n",
        "    result = load_and_predict(\"test_model\", input_data)\n",
        "    assert len(result) == 1\n",
        "    print(\"✓ Unit test PASSED for load_and_predict\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[Running unit test...]\")\n",
        "test_load_and_predict()"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### What static analysis would flag here\n",
        "\n",
        "Static analysis tools would look at the **code structure**, not just the test:\n",
        "- User input → file path → `open()` → `pickle.load()`\n",
        "- No sanitization, no allowlist, no checks.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is a classic **path traversal + unsafe deserialization** pattern.\n"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"\\n[What Static Analysis Would Flag:]\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  CRITICAL: Unsanitized user input in file path (model_name)\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  CRITICAL: Path traversal vulnerability\")\n",
        "print(\"    Example: model_name = '../../../etc/passwd'\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  CRITICAL: Unsafe pickle deserialization (arbitrary code execution)\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  WARNING: No authentication/authorization checks on model loading\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  WARNING: No rate limiting or access control\")\n",
        "print(\"\\n🔍 Static analysis sees dangerous patterns even when tests are green.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Cleanup\n",
        "os.remove(\"models/test_model.pkl\")\n",
        "os.rmdir(\"models\")"
      ]
    },

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */
    /* EXAMPLE 3: HARDCODED SECRETS & LOGGING SENSITIVE DATA         */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Example 3 — Configuration with Hardcoded Secrets\n",
        "\n",
        "### What this is meant to teach\n",
        "- Code can **work perfectly** while still leaking secrets.\n",
        "- Hardcoded API keys and passwords are a **major security smell**.\n",
        "- Logging secrets is a serious violation.\n",
        "\n",
        "We’ll define a `ModelConfig` class that passes tests but violates multiple security best practices.\n"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class ModelConfig:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Configuration for ML model deployment.\n",
        "    \n",
        "    ✅ PASSES TESTS: Works correctly in test environment.\n",
        "    ❌ SECURITY ISSUES: Hardcoded secrets, logging sensitive data.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self):\n",
        "        # Hardcoded credentials\n",
        "        self.api_key = \"sk-1234567890abcdef\"\n",
        "        self.db_password = \"MyP@ssw0rd123\"\n",
        "        self.log_file = \"/var/log/model.log\"\n",
        "        \n",
        "    def get_credentials(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Returns credentials for external API.\n",
        "        \n",
        "        ❌ Logs sensitive information.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        print(f\"Using API key: {self.api_key}\")\n",
        "        return self.api_key\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def connect_database(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Builds a database connection string.\"\"\"\n",
        "        connection_string = f\"postgresql://user:{self.db_password}@localhost/mldb\"\n",
        "        return connection_string\n",
        "\n",
        "def test_config():\n",
        "    \"\"\"Unit test passes because credentials exist and are non-empty.\"\"\"\n",
        "    config = ModelConfig()\n",
        "    assert config.api_key is not None\n",
        "    assert config.db_password is not None\n",
        "    assert len(config.get_credentials()) > 0\n",
        "    print(\"✓ Unit test PASSED for ModelConfig\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*70)\n",
        "print(\"EXAMPLE 3: CONFIGURATION MANAGEMENT\")\n",
        "print(\"=\"*70)\n",
        "print(\"\\n[Running unit test...]\")\n",
        "test_config()"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### What static analysis would flag here\n",
        "\n",
        "Static analysis tools scan **source code**, not runtime behavior:\n",
        "- They see hardcoded secrets.\n",
        "- They see secrets printed to logs.\n",
        "- They see credentials embedded in connection strings.\n",
        "\n",
        "All of this is invisible to normal unit tests.\n"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"\\n[What Static Analysis Would Flag:]\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  CRITICAL: Hardcoded API key in source code\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  CRITICAL: Hardcoded password in source code\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  CRITICAL: Sensitive data logged in plaintext\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  WARNING: Secrets not stored in environment variables or a vault\")\n",
        "print(\"⚠️  WARNING: Credentials embedded directly in connection string\")\n",
        "print(\"\\n🔍 Static analysis detects secret management violations that tests ignore.\")"
      ]
    },

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */
    /* SUMMARY: STATIC vs DYNAMIC ANALYSIS                           */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Static vs Dynamic Analysis — Why Both Matter\n",
        "\n",
        "Across all three examples:\n",
        "- ✅ Unit tests passed.\n",
        "- ✅ Code behaved correctly on test inputs.\n",
        "- ❌ Serious security issues were present in the code.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Why runtime tests missed these\n",
        "- Tests used **small, trusted data**.\n",
        "- Tests used **valid inputs only**.\n",
        "- Tests checked **functionality**, not **security properties**.\n",
        "\n",
        "### What static analysis adds\n",
        "- Looks at **all possible code paths**, not just those exercised in tests.\n",
        "- Flags **missing validation**, **unsafe patterns**, and **hardcoded secrets**.\n",
        "- Enforces **secure coding standards** across the codebase.\n"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*70)\n",
        "print(\"STATIC vs DYNAMIC ANALYSIS COMPARISON\")\n",
        "print(\"=\"*70)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nAll three code examples:\")\n",
        "print(\"  ✓ Passed unit tests\")\n",
        "print(\"  ✓ Worked correctly with test data\")\n",
        "print(\"  ✓ Would likely pass code review without security expertise\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nBut static analysis would find:\")\n",
        "print(\"  ⚠️  Missing input validation and data checks\")\n",
        "print(\"  ⚠️  Path traversal and unsafe deserialization\")\n",
        "print(\"  ⚠️  Hardcoded secrets and logging of sensitive data\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nKEY TAKEAWAY:\")\n",
        "print(\"Static analysis finds architectural and structural security gaps that\")\n",
        "print(\"runtime tests cannot see—especially in AI/ML code handling data, models,\")\n",
        "print(\"and secrets.\")\n",
        "print(\"=\"*70)"
      ]
    }

  ]
}

